# Editor-owned files — the Shopify theme editor is the source of truth for these,
# NOT git. They hold merchant-set section/theme settings (e.g. the funnel's Google
# Maps API key, Storefront token, prices, hero text). The repo's copies carry empty
# or stale values, so pushing them would overwrite live settings — this is exactly
# how the Maps key (address autocomplete + zone check) got wiped once already.
#
# The Shopify CLI honors this file on BOTH `theme push` and `theme pull`, for local
# runs and the CI workflows alike, so these paths are never overwritten by a deploy.
# Actual theme CODE (sections/*.liquid, snippets, assets, layout) still deploys.
config/settings_data.json
templates/*.json
